        "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ |\n\nLet $Y=-2X-2.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $a$ | $0$ | $b$ | $-4$ | $-6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $c$ | $d$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$",
